 text-observable in the baseline. I'm also considering the hasLoaded guard with onPageShow — sheet dismissal doesn't trigger that event, but navigating away and back would, and the guard prevents a reload in that case.\n\nI also notice if the first load fails, hasLoaded stays false so returning to the page re-triggers the request, and the same happens on app foregrounding. For PlayListPage, loadSongs lacks a guard against concurrent calls beyond button hiding, so rapid double-clicks could fire duplicate requests before the UI re-renders — it needs an isLoadingMore check. I'm also noting that currentOffset increments correctly on success but not on failure, and that HttpRequest's usingCache defaults to true since the constructor only sets it when truthy, meaning cached responses could be served for repeated identical URLs.\n\nOn error, HttpRequest shows a network error dialog after a delay, making page-level failures observable. The getSongsList function discards hasMore/songCount from the response, so I'll need to change its return type or add a new function in phase one. SongCard's sid uses index+1 for numbering, so appended songs should continue numbering from 31 onward as a good checkpoint to verify. ForEach lacks an explicit key generator, defaulting to index plus item JSON, which should still work fine even with duplicate songs across pages. Each SongCard also triggers its own picture URL request on appear, though that's unlikely to matter for test counting. Now I'm thinking about bottom spacing — the last ListItem has padding based on bottomRectHeight, and the load-more item needs to sit inside the List after the songs.\n\nFor scenario one, the spec requires no auto-loading on reaching the bottom — instead showing a \"click to load more\" prompt, so tests likely scroll to the end and verify no new request fires until the button is clicked, meaning the list stays at 30 items. For scenario two, pagination should use offset based on current list length, requesting the next batch of 30; though I'm uncertain whether the hidden test environment's API server will even be reachable, which could affect all search-related test points regardless of implementation. There's also ambiguity around how to show the loading state during \"load more\" — no exact text is specified, so I'm leaning toward reusing the SpinKit pattern similar to PlayListPage, though this remains unconfirmed.\n\nFor scenario three, determining when all results have loaded is unclear — I need to decide whether to rely on an API-provided `hasMore` flag, compare list length to total song count, or check whether the returned batch is smaller than the limit; combining `hasMore` with a fallback seems safest. I also need to verify the exact \"没有更多了~\" text matches character-for-character with what PlayListPage uses, including the tilde character encoding, and consider whether a first page with fewer than 30 results should immediately show this \"no more\" message.\n\nFor load-more failures, the list should remain intact and the \"点击加载更多\" trigger should reappear so the user can retry.\n\nOn rapid double-clicks, only one request should fire while loading is in progress—need a guard for that.\n\nThere's an edge case where the API reports hasMore=true but returns zero songs, possibly hitting a 600-song limit per the referenced issue—this would loop forever showing \"点击加载更多\" with nothing happening, so I should treat an empty returned list as hasMore=false regardless of what the API says.\n\n","startTime":1792321424289,"lastModifiedTime":1792321446661},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01FJo6dHyQA3yna72sXMm3a8","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"cd /Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec99 && grep -o '没有更多了.' spec/requirement.md | xxd | head -3; grep -o '没有更多了.' entry/src/main/ets/pages/PlayListPage.ets | xxd | head -2; grep -o '“点击加载更多”' spec/requirement.md | head -1 | xxd | head -2; grep -rn 'onSubmit\\|onReachEnd\\|LazyForEach\\|\\.id(\\|\\.key(' e